+## Current rule and authority
+
+Complete opposing boundary 4 endpoints activate an interior row or column. On their union, exchange 0↔8 and 6↔7 exactly once, including crossings; keep markers 4 fixed. The selected canonical rule remains `bce3d4596195`, exact Racket SHA-256 `5e8bc7939bbc421cafb04acc3034fae164476344c7aa36f1f9e6cf584171343d`. All four labeled canonical pairs remain accepted. The selected base target_code was synchronized to canonical whitespace through the public tool; archival raw_code and the canonical ledger are unchanged.
+
+## Decisions in version 4.0.0
+
+The prior sampler used one palette direction per grid. That leaves the global-direction rival indistinguishable on all 384 measured baseline inputs, even though mixed directions are validator-lawful. The new diagnostic slots contain both orientations, all four swappable values within exclusive row and column cells, crossings, and unpaired endpoints on all four sides. The exact Racket-labeled witness is `counterexamples/grid_wide_direction.json`; focused tests cover it through default seed 17/index 1.
+
+An eight-position default schedule alternates four resampled canonical shape/count/palette profiles with diagnostics. With three demonstrations and one query from four consecutive draws, any held-out position leaves a diagnostic visible. Twelve distinct rivals and six explicit witness implications are declared and tested. This finite support is not proof against every possible hypothesis. Exact overrides can remove witnesses; check actual assembled lessons with the hook.
+
+Canonical-profile slots remain available in every band. Diagnostics grow with difficulty and hard uses 30×30 on one quarter of default indices. Exact dimensions 6–30 by 8–30 and lane counts 0–4 are honored across bands, with declared texture incompatibilities. Strict controls reject coerced integers, bool/string cells, malformed grids, unknown keys/enumerations, and invalid density. The three named edge textures remain lawful; the no-anchor identity edge requires both field colors and no markers.
+
+Lane spacing is not a hard grammar requirement. The original sampler used unrestricted interior sampling, and the new one retains this behavior. Default field density is 0.35–0.55, with a finite exact-control range 0.1–0.7. Palette directions and witness positions are randomized within semantic constraints.
+
+## Runnable proposed extension
+
+`workspace/parametric/prototype.py` implements one episode-fixed parameter, `endpoint_threshold` in {1,2}. Default 2 returns exact canonical Racket; 1 activates a line at either endpoint. Public exports hide the parameter and query labels. Both settings use the same generated inputs. Two retained episodes distinguish the parameter in every demo and all query rotations, and default Racket reproduces all four canonical labels. This is a proposed prototype only, with no production or training approval.
+
+## Verification and open finding
+
+Final generator SHA-256: `450d238a82ab2de4b6c808f5f70f966a1667cbdcbf952cf322a826d5dcc51e1d`.
+
+Final strict battery: eleven green stages, one failed stage. Semantic checks pass: four canonical pairs accepted, six witness claims verified, twelve smoke lessons identifiable, zero ambiguous query rotations out of 48. The remaining strict defect-lint warning is exact finite-set `object_count` disjointness. The task-local read-only `workspace/probe_structure.py` reproduces it without changing sampler or gate. Canonical train counts {4,12,32} are absent from the lint cohort; overlapping ranges are not evidence of distribution equality. Acceptance needs a maintainer decision on this coarse statistic, and is not claimed routine.
+
+`workspace/probe_curriculum.py` produces exact source-bound Racket cases and dynamically enumerates actual rivals; its separate input-only size census has an explicit label policy. Full command receipts, earlier failed iterations, final lesson/schedule counts, audit results, and fresh replay tests are in the returned review evidence. Approvals and other tasks were not changed.
